-- title:
--   Kernel of a diamond pull-back action is ±Γ_H(M)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, $M$ a nonzero natural number and $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ a subgroup. Write $\Gamma_H(M)$ for [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ obtained as the image, under the inclusion of $\Gamma_0(M)$, of the preimage of $H$ under the homomorphism [`CohCarrier.gamma0Units`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L121) sending $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M)$ to the unit of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ given by the reduction of its lower‑right entry (with inverse the reduction of its upper‑left entry). Write $\bar F =$ [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC K (CohCarrier.GammaH M H)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) for the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $K((q))$ generated over $K$ by all quotients $\bar p_f/\bar p_g$, where $f,g$ are modular forms of one and the same weight $k$ on $\Gamma_H(M)$ (viewed in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$), $p_f,p_g$ are power series over $\mathbb{Z}$ whose complex images are the $q$-expansions of $f,g$, $\bar p$ denotes the coefficientwise reduction to $K$ viewed as a Laurent series, and $\bar p_g \ne 0$. Let $\rho$ be a homomorphism from $\Gamma_0(M)$ to the group of $K$-algebra automorphisms of $\bar F$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.IsDiamondPullbackModL`](def/ModularCurve_XHDiamondModL.html#L12): for every $\delta \in \Gamma_0(M)$, every weight $k$, all forms $f,g,f_1,g_1$ of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_H(M)$ with integral expansions $p_f,p_g,p_{f_1},p_{g_1}$, with $f_1 = f\mid_k\delta$ and $g_1 = g\mid_k\delta$ as functions on the upper half-plane and $\bar p_g \ne 0$, every element $x$ of $\bar F$ whose underlying Laurent series is $\bar p_{f_1}/\bar p_{g_1}$ has $\rho(\delta)(x)$ with underlying Laurent series $\bar p_f/\bar p_g$. Then for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M)$ one has $\rho(\gamma) = 1$ if and only if [`CohCarrier.gamma0Units M γ`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L121) lies in the subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ generated by $H$ together with $-1$.
--
--   This is the faithfulness statement for the diamond operators acting on the reduction of the function field of $X_H(M)$: the pull-back formula alone forces the kernel of $\rho$ to be exactly $\pm\Gamma_H(M)$, so that $\rho$ induces a faithful action of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times/\langle H, -1\rangle$ on $\bar F$. It is used in the identification of the modular function field and of Galois/inertia quotients attached to $X_0(p)$ and $X_1$ models; the only input quoted is the family of weight‑four partial‑divisor‑sum Eisenstein series on $\Gamma_1(M)$ with prescribed integral $q$-expansions and diamond transformation behaviour.
